@startuml seq-05-deny
!include style.iuml
title Deny: refused without asking, and the races Deny can be in\n(Deny > Always > Ask > default; C1, C3, C4, C9, C13; H-082, H-085, H-086, H-118, H-126)
autonumber "<b>0."

participant "Agent Mara\n(model)" as Agent
participant "wallet~__send\n(EffectTool)" as Tool
database "Store" as Store
participant "Web app" as Web
actor Owner
participant "Wallet lane" as Lane
participant "Signer" as Signer
participant "RPC / Base" as Chain

group A. Deny set ahead refuses in words, with no Wait
  Agent -> Tool : wallet~__send {to: Bob, amount: "3"}
  Tool -> Store : admission commit: the allowed hook reads the Recipients doc:\nDeny(wallet, Bob), checked before covering looks for Always
  note right of Store
    row: payment Idle · call [wallet_usable and payer == 'agent' and eff == 'deny'] → Refused.
    Deny beats an open Always (banda-integration rules check).
  end note
  Tool --> Agent : "wallet~__send did not run: the owner doesn't pay Bob."
end

group B. "Never pay" on a card sets Deny and sweeps
  Owner -> Web : card for 0x77e0…: name "Spam", Never pay
  Web -> Store : answer {wait, refuse, never, label "Spam", version v}
  note right of Store
    fill commit: Deny(wallet, 0x77e0…) in the Recipients doc;
    this payment Refused; every other open ask and queued payment
    it covers refused in the same commit (C9)
    rows: recipient · card_never [version_current] → deny;
    payment Waiting · card_never [payer == 'agent'] → Refused
  end note
end

group C. Deny committed while a payment is queued (the race with the lane)
  Lane -> Signer : sign I (to Carol), nonce = ledger.next
  Owner -> Web : Recipients → Carol → Deny
  Web -> Store : set rule {Carol, deny, version v}
  alt the Deny commit lands first (commit order decides, C1)
    note right of Store
      Deny commit: payment Queued · deny_committed [payer == 'agent'] → Refused
      (Deny's sweep, C9); recipient · list_set_deny [version_current] → deny
    end note
    Signer --> Lane : raw bytes
    Lane -> Store : start commit: I is no longer Queued
    note right of Store : the bytes are dropped; no nonce burnt; nothing signed after the Deny counts (C4, H-118)
    Store --> Agent : "Not paid: the owner doesn't pay Carol"
  else the start commit lands first
    Signer --> Lane : raw bytes
    Lane -> Store : start commit: I → Signed (burn point)
    Store -> Store : Deny commit: Signed · deny_committed → Signed (C13)
    Lane -> Chain : broadcast stored bytes
    note right of Store
      Past the burn point the payment finishes and is reported;
      the Deny applies from the next payment (H-085).
    end note
    Store --> Agent : "may have sent" until a receipt decides, then "Paid Carol 4 USDC"
  end
end

group D. A crash, then a Deny, then the tool's rerun (H-126)
  Lane -> Chain : broadcast stored bytes of I
  note over Lane : the daemon is killed here
  Owner -> Web : Deny Carol (after the restart, before the rerun)
  Tool -> Store : idempotent rerun under the same key
  note right of Store
    Stored bytes exist for the key: the rerun reaches run, which only
    rebroadcasts and reports the lane's outcome; never "did not run"
    (C13; banda-integration "killed after-broadcast-deny").
  end note
  Tool --> Agent : the lane's outcome: "Paid Carol" once a receipt decides
end
@enduml
